# 1. Executive Summary & Core Principles

## 1.1. Product Vision

The **Football Analytics Platform** is a web-based data application designed to deliver multi-layered football intelligence across competitions, seasons, matches, teams, players, and individual pitch events.

Unlike generic live-score dashboards that present static tabular tallies, this platform establishes a robust, event-driven data engineering pipeline:

```text
[External Data APIs] ──► [Ingestion Workers] ──► [Kafka Streaming] ──► [MinIO (Raw Data Lake)]
                                                                                │
[AI Football Analyst] ◄── [Next.js App] ◄── [FastAPI API] ◄── [ClickHouse] ◄───┘ (ETL / dbt)
```

> **Target Identity:**  
> A dedicated analytical intelligence suite for football—merging modern data warehouse speeds with deterministic AI insights.

---

## 1.2. The Golden Engineering Rule: Data as Source of Truth

The foundational design tenet of the entire platform is:

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│             CLICKHOUSE ANALYTICAL DATABASE             │
│            (Single Authoritative Data Truth)           │
└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                           │
                           ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│               DETERMINISTIC ANALYTICS API              │
│            (Validated SQL Queries & Bounds)            │
└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                           │
                           ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   AI FOOTBALL ANALYST                  │
│       (Interprets, Synthesizes & Communicates)         │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Zero Tolerance for Hallucinations:**  
> The system must always be capable of answering: *"Where did this exact number come from?"*  
> The LLM is **never** permitted to generate freeform SQL directly against the analytical database, nor invent statistical metrics. All numerical claims originate from strictly validated tool calls.

---

## 1.3. Engineering Objectives by Domain

| Domain | Key Capabilities Demonstrated |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Backend Engineering** | REST API clean architecture, modular monolith, Pydantic validation, JWT auth, Redis multi-tier caching, query optimization, rate limiting, structured logging, background tasks. |
| **Data Engineering** | Multi-source ingestion, event streaming (Kafka/Redpanda), raw lake storage (S3/MinIO), idempotency, ClickHouse OLAP modeling, dbt SQL transformations, data quality testing, DLQ, Kestra orchestration. |
| **AI Engineering** | LangGraph agentic workflows, deterministic tool-calling, intent recognition, contextual synthesis, strict hallucination guardrails, conversational state management. |
| **Frontend Engineering** | Next.js App Router, SSR/CSR balance, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui design system, Recharts, SVG/D3 dynamic pitch visualization (shot maps & heatmaps), responsive UX. |

---

## 1.4. Target Users

- **Casual Football Enthusiasts:** Seeking deep answers to player form, season-over-season progression, and squad attack profiles.
- **Data-Oriented Football Fans:** Requiring advanced metrics (xG, xA, PPDA, pass completion under pressure, shot locations, progressive metrics).
- **Recruiters & Engineers:** Assessing a clean production-grade architecture spanning event streaming, data warehousing, and AI orchestration.

---

## 1.5. Product Scope & Non-Goals

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                 IN SCOPE                                     │
├───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────┤
│ Competition & Match   │ Player & Team Analytics      │ AI & Data Platform    │
│ • Match schedules     │ • Profiles & radar metrics   │ • Natural language Q&A│
│ • Full lineups & score│ • Historical comparisons     │ • Kafka streaming     │
│ • Shot & pass events  │ • Interactive pitch shot maps│ • ClickHouse OLAP     │
└───────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────┘
```

> [!WARNING]
> **Explicit Non-Goals for Initial Release:**  
> Live match video streaming, betting/gambling integrations, social networking feeds, user-generated blogs, fantasy football games, real-time millisecond ball tracking, complex proprietary ML xG training (use provider xG first).

