## 2.2. Vercel vs. Dedicated Worker Runtime Separation

To prevent timeout failures, memory limits, and socket leakage, workloads are strictly partitioned:

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐    ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         VERCEL APPLICATION EDGE            │    │         DEDICATED COMPUTE WORKERS          │
│    (Next.js App, Serverless BFF & CDN)     │    │   (Railway, Render, Fly.io, or AWS ECS)    │
├────────────────────────────────────────────┤    ├────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ • Next.js React Server Components & UI     │    │ • Continuous Kafka consumer loops          │
│ • Server-Side Rendering (SSR) & Static CDN │    │ • Heavy, long-running ETL & backfill jobs  │
│ • Client Session & Auth callbacks          │    │ • Ingestion crawlers & external API polling│
│ • Short-lived REST & AI streaming proxies  │    │ • ClickHouse bulk stream ingestion         │
└────────────────────────────────────────────┘    └────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 2.3. Technology Stack Matrix

| Tier | Primary Technology | Justification & Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Web Frontend** | Next.js 15, TypeScript, React 19 | SSR/SSG flexibility, modern React Server Components, developer velocity. |
| **UI Design System** | Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui | Modern, responsive dark-mode aesthetics with accessible headless primitives. |
| **Visualizations** | Recharts + SVG / D3.js | Interactive trend charts, pitch radar diagrams, and coordinate-precise shot maps. |
| **Backend Framework** | FastAPI (Python 3.11+) | Asynchronous execution, native Pydantic OpenAPI docs, rich data ecosystem. |
| **Transactional DB** | PostgreSQL 16 | Relational consistency for users, permissions, saved searches, and metadata. |
| **Analytical DB** | ClickHouse | Columnar OLAP engine capable of querying millions of events with sub-second latency. |
| **In-Memory Cache** | Redis 7 | API response caching, rate limiting tokens, and temporary AI conversation states. |
| **Event Streaming** | Apache Kafka / Redpanda | Decoupled streaming pipelines, durable message logs, and replay capabilities. |
| **Raw Storage** | MinIO (local) / S3 (cloud) | Immutable bronze data lake preserving original JSON payloads. |
| **Transformations** | Python + dbt | Python for data normalization; dbt for modeling, SQL DAGs, and data tests. |
| **Orchestration** | Kestra | Declarative workflow runner for batch ingestion, daily syncs, and aggregate refreshes. |
| **AI Orchestration** | LangGraph + OpenAI / Claude | Deterministic state graph, tool call loops, and conversational memory. |

